---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How affiliate links and commercial relationships work on A Rap Blog."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language disclosure</p>
      <h1>Recommendations stay independent.</h1>
      <p>Here is exactly how A Rap Blog may make money from links.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell legal-copy">
      <p class="status-note">
        Some publications may contain affiliate links. If you make a purchase through one of those
        links, A Rap Blog may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
      </p>
      <h2>How links are labeled</h2>
      <p>
        Every publication containing monetized links displays a disclosure before the first such link.
        Links may also carry a short descriptive label. The phrase “affiliate link” by itself is
        not treated as sufficient explanation.
      </p>
      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>
        Compensation does not determine whether an album, book, or product is recommended.
        Research and writing happen before merchant links are added. A higher commission does not
        improve a recommendation’s position.
      </p>
      <h2>Current and future programs</h2>
      <p>
        The initial commercial program is expected to be Bookshop.org. If other programs are
        introduced, their required disclosures will be added here and in the relevant publications.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If a relationship is unclear, please contact the publication through the address on the
        <a href="/about">about page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
